WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.360
YieldShield on Monad gives your crypto
position two ways to exit.

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.670
Keep the remaining asset, or exchange the
position for an eligible backing

3
00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.580
payout. Let's walk through how the two
sides of a pool fit together.

4
00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:18.037
Start at the faucet. You'll need testnet
MON for network fees, plus

5
00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:23.687
the asset you want to use. The app
supports wrapped MON and staked MON.

6
00:00:24.497 --> 00:00:28.827
Everything shown here runs on testnet with
valueless test assets.

7
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.800
Choose Protect, pick a pool, and enter an
amount.

8
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.310
Review the backing token, available
capacity, gain-sharing fees, and

9
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.520
waiting period before confirming in your
wallet.

10
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.160
Your position then appears under
Positions, where you can manage its exits.

11
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.180
Here's a simple example. A $100 asset has
$150 of backing.

12
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.780
If the asset falls 20%, taking the asset
leaves $80.

13
00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:01.190
The eligible backing exit pays $100
instead, and the pool receives the

14
00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.340
surrendered asset.

15
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:05.757
Now, let the asset rise 20%.

16
00:01:05.757 --> 00:01:09.907
In this example, fees take 12% of the $20
gain.

17
00:01:10.657 --> 00:01:13.927
That leaves $117.60 in asset value.

18
00:01:14.637 --> 00:01:16.607
You can compare both exits before
choosing.

19
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:20.633
Backing providers supply the pool's first-
loss capital.

20
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:25.143
They earn a share of realized gains and
take the downside when backing is

21
00:01:25.143 --> 00:01:30.583
used. In our falling price example, their
$150 becomes $130

22
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.253
in illustrative residual value.

23
00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:39.097
Protection has limits. Caps are measured
in backing tokens, not guaranteed

24
00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:44.077
cash. Waiting periods and withdrawal
conditions apply, and fees already

25
00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:46.787
realized aren't refunded after a later
loss.

26
00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:50.447
Smart contract pricing and token risks
remain.

27
00:01:51.557 --> 00:01:54.367
The calculator is an illustration, not a
live quote.

28
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:59.243
Ready to explore? Get test tokens, compare
the pools, and try the

29
00:01:59.243 --> 00:02:01.653
calculator on how it works. Your asset.

30
00:02:02.263 --> 00:02:03.453
Separately supplied backing.

31
00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:06.893
Two ways to exit. YieldShield on Monad.
